    {
      "title": "Sample order, history, counts and lifecycle",
      "contract": {
        "fresh": "Fresh prefix64 doubles equals first Float32 widened, or zero for NULL; input begins storage[64], logical consumed counter starts64. Fresh flag clears even on a zero call.",
        "later": "Input begins storage[128], logical consumed counter starts0. Working sample center always restarts storage[64].",
        "terminal": "Append64 copies of the positive call last Float32 frame, or zero for NULL/zero call. Local input limit increases64; cumulative real input does not.",
        "phase": "While trunc_i64(phase)>=512 and logical index<local limit: phase=RN64(phase-512); increment logical index and every channel center. Then emit a whole channel frame if logical index<limit; phase=RN64(phase+step); repeat.",
        "left_taps": "m=trunc_i32(phase); f=RN64(phase-Double(m)); acc=+0; for k0..63, w=FMA(f,d[m+512k],h[m+512k]); acc=FMA(center[-k],w,acc).",
        "right_taps": "q=RN64(512-phase); m=trunc_i32(q); f=RN64(q-Double(m)); for k0..63, w=FMA(f,d[m+512k],h[m+512k]); acc=FMA(center[k+1],w,acc). Only then narrow Float32.",
        "carry": "Copy128 doubles starting center-64 into each buffer beginning. Storage outside copied region is retained.",
        "count": "Always add generated frames to cumulative generated. Terminal target=trunc_i64(RN64(ratio*Double(cumulative real input))); if target<new cumulative generated, return max(current generated+target-new cumulative generated,0); otherwise return current generated. Retained generated counter is not reduced.",
        "reset": "0x10030aeb8 clears phase and both native counters, sets fresh1; it does not clear storage/tables. Destroy/create is required for a genuinely fresh reconstruction seek.",
        "resize": "For caller n>capacity, packet changes capacity=n+1024 then reallocates zero-filled channel buffers, without resetting phase/counters/fresh. Fixed channel count subset avoids reconfiguration/free-count uncertainty.",
        "partition": "Short first blocks are supported and may retain zero/stale gaps. No partition invariance is asserted."
      },
